<main>

<!-- ===================== START & REVIEW ===================== -->
<section class="view" id="v-start" data-title="Start here">
  <div class="page" data-key="home" data-label="Start">
    <div class="head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Pre-lesson & Chapter Guide</p>
      <h1>Discrete Probability Distributions</h1>
      <p class="lead">From individual trials to continuous intervals: Master the <strong>Bernoulli</strong>, <strong>Binomial</strong>, and <strong>Poisson</strong> models across all 16 textbook examples.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="lab">
      <div class="svgwrap">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 540 180" role="img" aria-label="Overview of Bernoulli, Binomial, and Poisson">
          <!-- Bernoulli -->
          <rect x="40" y="110" width="18" height="40" class="bar-v"/>
          <rect x="70" y="70" width="18" height="80" class="bar-v"/>
          <line class="axis" x1="20" x2="110" y1="150" y2="150"/>
          <text class="lbl-s" x="49" y="165" text-anchor="middle">0</text>
          <text class="lbl-s" x="79" y="165" text-anchor="middle">1</text>
          <text class="vt" x="65" y="35" text-anchor="middle">Bernoulli</text>
          <text class="lbl-s" x="65" y="52" text-anchor="middle">1 trial</text>

          <!-- Binomial -->
          <rect x="180" y="130" width="14" height="20" class="bar-v"/>
          <rect x="200" y="90" width="14" height="60" class="bar-v"/>
          <rect x="220" y="60" width="14" height="90" class="bar-v"/>
          <rect x="240" y="80" width="14" height="70" class="bar-v"/>
          <rect x="260" y="120" width="14" height="30" class="bar-v"/>
          <line class="axis" x1="165" x2="295" y1="150" y2="150"/>
          <text class="vt" x="230" y="35" text-anchor="middle">Binomial B(n, p)</text>
          <text class="lbl-s" x="230" y="52" text-anchor="middle">n independent trials</text>

          <!-- Poisson -->
          <path d="M 370 140 Q 400 30 430 80 T 500 150" fill="none" stroke="var(--amber)" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/>
          <circle cx="370" cy="140" r="4" class="bar-a"/>
          <circle cx="395" cy="70" r="4" class="bar-a"/>
          <circle cx="420" cy="65" r="4" class="bar-a"/>
          <circle cx="445" cy="90" r="4" class="bar-a"/>
          <circle cx="470" cy="125" r="4" class="bar-a"/>
          <circle cx="495" cy="145" r="4" class="bar-a"/>
          <line class="axis" x1="350" x2="520" y1="150" y2="150"/>
          <text class="vt" x="435" y="35" text-anchor="middle">Poisson Po(λ)</text>
          <text class="lbl-s" x="435" y="52" text-anchor="middle">Rate in continuous space</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </div>
    <h2>Curriculum Learning Targets</h2>
    <div class="defn">
      <p>• <strong>LU 11.1 / 12.1:</strong> Recognise Bernoulli, Binomial, and Poisson probability functions.</p>
      <p>• <strong>LU 12.2:</strong> Compute and apply their expectations and variances: \(E(X)\) and \(\operatorname{Var}(X)\).</p>
      <p>• <strong>LU 12.3:</strong> Formulate layered decision models and sequential stopping rules.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="page" data-key="review" data-label="Quick Review">
    <div class="head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Prerequisites</p>
      <h1>Total Probability & Bayes' Theorem</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="defn">
      <span class="lbl">Law of Total Probability</span>
      \[P(B) = \sum_{i=1}^n P(A_i \cap B) = \sum_{i=1}^n P(A_i)P(B|A_i)\]
      <span class="lbl" style="margin-top:8px">Bayes' Theorem</span>
      \[P(A_k|B) = \frac{P(A_k \cap B)}{P(B)} = \frac{P(A_k)P(B|A_k)}{\sum_{i=1}^n P(A_i)P(B|A_i)}\]
    </div>
    <details class="note tip" open><summary><span class="lb">Crucial Link for Chapter 10</span></summary><div class="body">
      <p>Many multi-step exam questions in Chapter 10 require you to calculate probabilities using Binomial or Poisson models first, and then apply Bayes' theorem to reverse the condition.</p>
    </div></details>
  </div>
