<!-- ===================== BERNOULLI ===================== -->
<section class="view" id="v-bern" data-title="Bernoulli Distribution" hidden>
  <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Section 10.1A</p><h1>Bernoulli Distribution</h1></div>

  <div class="page" data-key="idea" data-label="Concepts">
    <p>A <span class="term">Bernoulli trial</span> is an experiment with exactly two outcomes: <em>success</em> (\(X=1\)) with probability \(p\), and <em>failure</em> (\(X=0\)) with probability \(1-p\).</p>
    <div class="defn">
      <span class="lbl">Probability Function</span>
      \[P(X=x) = p^x (1-p)^{1-x} \quad \text{for } x = 0, 1\]
      <hr style="border:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin:8px 0">
      <p><strong>Mean and Variance:</strong></p>
      \[\mu = E(X) = p \qquad\text{and}\qquad \sigma^2 = \operatorname{Var}(X) = p(1-p)\]
    </div>

    <!-- Real-life Bernoulli Experiments Simulation -->
    <div class="lab">
      <div class="lab-h"><span class="tag teal">Interactive Experiment</span><h3>Everyday Bernoulli Trials</h3></div>
      <p class="small muted">Random experiments with only two possible outcomes are Bernoulli trials. Select an experiment and simulate it:</p>
      <div class="row">
        <button class="btn primary" id="btnExpCoin">Coin Toss (Head / Tail)</button>
        <button class="btn" id="btnExpTarget">Target Shot (Hit / Miss)</button>
        <button class="btn" id="btnExpQC">Manufactured Item (Defective / Normal)</button>
        <button class="btn" id="btnExpMC">Guessing 4-Choice MC (Correct / Incorrect)</button>
      </div>
