<!-- ===================== BINOMIAL ===================== -->
<section class="view" id="v-bino" data-title="Binomial Distribution B(n, p)" hidden>
  <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Section 10.1B & C</p><h1>Binomial Distribution <i>B</i>(<i>n</i>, <i>p</i>)</h1></div>

  <div class="page" data-key="idea" data-label="Concepts">
    <p>When a Bernoulli trial with success probability \(p\) is repeated \(n\) times <strong>independently</strong>, the number of successes \(X\) is a binomial variable:</p>
    <div class="defn">
      <span class="lbl">Binomial Distribution \(B(n, p)\)</span>
      \[P(X=x) = C_x^n p^x (1-p)^{n-x} \quad \text{for } x = 0, 1, 2, \dots, n\]
      <hr style="border:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin:8px 0">
      <p><strong>Mean and Variance:</strong></p>
      \[\mu = E(X) = np \qquad\text{and}\qquad \sigma^2 = \operatorname{Var}(X) = np(1-p)\]
    </div>

    <!-- Derivation based on Class Activity 10.1 -->
    <details class="note tip" open><summary><span class="lb">Derivation</span> How we derive the Binomial Formula (Class Activity 10.1)</summary><div class="body">
      <p>Consider tossing a coin \(n=3\) times where \(P(\text{Head}) = p\) and \(P(\text{Tail}) = 1-p\):</p>
      <ol style="margin:0;padding-left:1.3em;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px">
        <li>Any single specific outcome with \(x\) heads and \((n-x)\) tails (e.g. \(H, T, T\)) has probability \(p^x (1-p)^{n-x}\) because trials are independent.</li>
        <li>How many ways can we arrange \(x\) heads among \(n\) trials? This is equivalent to putting \(x\) letters \(H\) into \(n\) ordered slots: \(C_x^n\) ways.</li>
        <li>Multiplying the count of ways by the probability of each way yields:
          \[P(X=x) = C_x^n p^x (1-p)^{n-x}\]
        </li>
        <li><strong>Sum of probabilities:</strong> By the Binomial Theorem:
          \[\sum_{x=0}^n P(X=x) = \sum_{x=0}^n C_x^n p^x (1-p)^{n-x} = [p + (1-p)]^n = 1^n = 1\]
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div></details>

    <!-- Guided Exploration -->
    <div class="lab">
      <div class="lab-h"><span class="tag teal">Interactive Exploration</span><h3>Distribution Shape & Skewness</h3></div>
      
